.TH MDT.ENABLE_PARALLEL_RENAME_REMOTE 4 2026-09-25 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdt.enable_parallel_rename_remote \- parallel rename of remote-source files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.RI "lctl get_param mdt." FSNAME *.enable_parallel_rename_remote
.SY
.RI "lctl set_param mdt." FSNAME *.enable_parallel_rename_remote= ENABLE
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR 644 | -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present for MDT devices.
.TP
.B Default
.RB enable_parallel_rename_remote= 1
.SH DESCRIPTION
The boolean
.B enable_parallel_rename_remote
parameter controls whether renaming a non-directory may proceed without
the filesystem-wide rename lock when the source parent directory or the
source object is located on another MDT.
.PP
The rename lock is an exclusive lock on a single resource held for the
duration of the distributed transaction, so taking it serialises every
such rename across the whole filesystem and limits the aggregate rate to
a few hundred per second regardless of how many MDTs are configured.
Renaming a non-directory cannot create a directory loop, which is what
the rename lock exists to prevent, so it is not required for this case.
If
.I ENABLE
is
.B 1
(or aliases
.BR on " or " true ),
these renames are permitted to run in parallel. If it is
.B 0
or
.B off
they take the rename lock as before.
.PP
During a rolling upgrade, keep this parameter at
.B 0
until every MDT runs a release that has it: a directory migration on an
MDT running an older release relies on the rename lock to keep these
renames out.
.PP
This parameter applies only to non-directories. A directory rename
takes the rename lock whenever the two parents differ or the source
parent is on another MDT, since it can change the directory hierarchy;
a same-directory rename of a directory whose object alone is remote
does not, and is governed by
.BR enable_parallel_rename_dir .
.PP
Three parameters apply to the rename of a non-directory, and it takes
the rename lock unless every one of them that applies permits it.
.B enable_parallel_rename_file
governs every non-directory rename, so setting it to
.B 0
also disables the behaviour described here.
.B enable_parallel_rename_crossdir
governs those that cross directories, including remote ones, so
setting it to
.B 0
disables this behaviour for a cross-directory rename but not for a
same-directory one. This parameter governs renames whose source parent
or source object is on another MDT.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following module:
.EX
.B mdt.*.enable_parallel_rename_remote
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Disable parallel rename of files with a remote source on the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB "mgs# " "lctl set_param -P mdt.testfs-*.enable_parallel_rename_remote=0"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B enable_parallel_rename_remote
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_58
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mdt.enable_parallel_rename_crossdir (4),
.BR mdt.enable_parallel_rename_dir (4),
.BR mdt.enable_parallel_rename_file (4),
.BR mdt.enable_remote_dir (4),
.BR mdt.rename_stats (4),
.BR lustre (7),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
